From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:42:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] proxy: allow direct Rust trap callbacks on embedder handlers

Host-owned bridge proxies forward every property read, write, has check,
and function call to native Rust. Going through JS handler property lookup,
index stringification, and temporary argument arrays adds overhead on every
crossing; HostProxyTraps lets those handlers dispatch directly while
preserving Proxy invariant checks whenever the target has own properties.
